text.section:
Notwithstanding any provision of § 38.2-3432.2, 38.2-3501, 38.2-4306, or any other section of this title to the contrary, a health carrier offering a health benefit plan providing individual or small group health insurance coverage shall develop its premium rates based on the following:

Whether the health benefit plan covers an individual or family;


Rating areas, as may be established by the Commission;


Age, except that the rate shall not vary by more than 3 to 1 for adults; and


Tobacco use, except that the rate shall not vary by more than 1.5 to 1.
